    "conclusion": {
     "summary": "### Language Transition Summary\n\nFor Burkina Faso students, the greatest challenge at ALA is language transition rather than intellectual capability or academic potential.\n\nAcross all subjects analysed, students demonstrate:\n\n- Strong resilience\n- Strong work ethic\n- Strong awareness of African development issues\n- Good analytical reasoning\n- Strong social and environmental awareness\n- Strong academic discipline\n\nHowever, the transition from a French-medium educational system to an highly rigorous English-medium Cambridge curriculum can initially affect:\n\n- Academic writing\n- Research communication\n- Classroom participation\n- Leadership communication\n- Presentations\n- Debate participation\n- Independent inquiry",
