      "title": "Comparative Language Analysis",
      "body": "| Area | Tunisia | Burkina Faso |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| French Literacy | Very High | High |\n| Academic Writing | High | Moderate-High |\n| English Exposure | Moderate | Low-Moderate |\n| Research Writing Readiness | Moderate | Low-Moderate |\n| Classroom Participation in English | Moderate | Moderate-Low |\n| Presentation Skills | Moderate | Moderate |\n| Overall Language Transition Readiness | Moderate | Moderate-Low |\n\n### Key Observation\n\nCompared to Tunisia, Burkina Faso students generally face a larger English-language transition challenge.\n\nThis is not because of lower academic ability, but because:\n\n- English exposure is typically lower.\n- Academic resources are more frequently available only in French.\n- Research and presentation opportunities are often more limited.\n- Students have fewer opportunities to engage in English-medium academic environments before ALA."
